    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0309" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v03/pg283"/>

                <head>115. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Vietnam<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d115-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1963-05-09T15:24:00-04:00">May 9, 1963, 3:24
                        p.m.</date></hi></dateline></opener>
                <p>1066. Hue 4 to Dept.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d115-f2"/> At your discretion suggest
                    you urge GVN take no repressive measures against Buddhists, offer sympathy and
                    funeral expenses to families of demonstration victims, make any other
                    appropriate gestures toward restoration of order and amity between religious
                    groups.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d115-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d115-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, SOC 14-1 S VIET. Secret; Operational
                    Immediate. Drafted by Heavner and cleared by Rice. Repeated to CINCPAC for
                    POLAD.</p>
            </note>
